WEBVTT

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:10.900
Yugi Muto assembled the Millennium Puzzle 
and became the guardian of the Shadow Games.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:17.260
Pegasus has a Millennium Item 
of his own - the Millennium Eye.

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:21.800
Yugi accepts Pegasus's challenge 
and goes to Duelist Kingdom.

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:28.010
Pegasus stole his grandfather Sugoroku's 
soul, and Yugi intends to rescue him.

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:33.850
He battles alongside his trusted 
friends and with his other self.

00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:44.300
I can't finish reading the magazine pages

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:51.210
I get the feeling that I must read it

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:57.960
Game cartridges are stacked 
in the corner of the room

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:04.660
Is there no meaning if I don't play them?

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:09.760
You're on the other side of the table

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:13.130
I'm talking to you, but...

00:01:13.730 --> 00:01:20.060
You don't change your 
facial expression at all

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:26.310
Even though I'm this close to you

00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:33.580
These feelings don't reach 
you, don't reach you

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:40.320
What is truly precious?

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:47.310
This spell card swaps 
attack and defense points!

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:54.730
The Zombies have 0 attack points!

00:01:54.970 --> 00:01:56.880
Here I go, you zombie freak!

00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:59.600
Ultimate Screw Knuckle!

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:02.430
Jonouchi!

00:02:02.610 --> 00:02:04.340
I did it, Yugi.

00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:05.650
Let's go.

00:02:05.650 --> 00:02:06.680
Boss...

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:09.650
What?

00:02:12.110 --> 00:02:15.940
Now they'll never get out of the cave!

00:02:18.020 --> 00:02:24.040
Labyrinth Tag Duel

00:02:33.330 --> 00:02:35.600
Damn!  It won't even budge!

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:38.250
We have to find another exit.

00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:41.600
How are we supposed to do that?

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:42.930
Well...

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:45.730
Bakura?

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:52.530
I think Pegasus's castle is this way.

00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:53.920
Why?

00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:55.930
Let's go.

00:03:20.330 --> 00:03:21.730
Big brother...

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:28.730
Don't worry about me.

00:03:29.150 --> 00:03:32.000
I'm fine.

00:03:33.260 --> 00:03:37.660
You always protected me.

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:53.640
When we were together, I 
always had a great time.

00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:55.330
Always.

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:09.730
I want to see you, big brother.

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:16.130
Bakura, are you sure this is the right way?

00:04:16.130 --> 00:04:17.860
We've been walking for a while.

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:21.060
And the path is getting narrower.

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:23.800
The walls look different too.

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:28.330
They used to be rough, but not anymore.

00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:31.050
This is definitely man-made.

00:04:31.050 --> 00:04:35.220
It feels like we're walking in a maze.

00:04:39.690 --> 00:04:41.330
What's going on?

00:04:41.330 --> 00:04:42.860
Which way should we go?

00:04:42.860 --> 00:04:43.930
This way.

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:45.800
The exit is this way!

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:47.530
Bakura, wait up!

00:04:47.530 --> 00:04:49.400
Are you okay, Bakura?

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:51.240
Is this really the right way?

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:58.530
What is it?

00:05:11.690 --> 00:05:13.600
What's up with this room?

00:05:27.130 --> 00:05:28.060
We are...

00:05:28.060 --> 00:05:29.800
...guardians of the underground dungeon.

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:33.060
We are the Labyrinth Brothers.

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:34.730
Labyrinth Brothers?

00:05:34.730 --> 00:05:37.400
Is this a Hong Kong action movie?

00:05:39.050 --> 00:05:42.330
They have Star Chips!  They 
must be Player Killers!

00:05:42.330 --> 00:05:46.000
It's been awhile since travelers 
got lost inside the labyrinth.

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:49.330
But it wouldn't be a labyrinth 
if you didn't get lost.

00:05:50.060 --> 00:05:54.130
Lost ones, you wish to 
learn the correct path.

00:05:54.530 --> 00:05:55.960
The correct path.

00:05:55.960 --> 00:05:56.970
In that case...

00:05:56.970 --> 00:05:58.140
...if you want to know the answer...

00:05:58.360 --> 00:06:00.800
Defeat us in a duel!

00:06:02.820 --> 00:06:04.800
Is that a Duel Ring?

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:11.820
One of those doors leads to the correct path.

00:06:11.820 --> 00:06:14.480
If you defeat us, you get to choose one.

00:06:14.480 --> 00:06:18.320
If you do not escape, you will 
wander the labyrinth for eternity.

00:06:18.530 --> 00:06:23.230
So if we don't win this 
duel, we can never leave?

00:06:23.230 --> 00:06:26.710
This duel will be a special two-on-two match.

00:06:26.710 --> 00:06:29.110
Two duelists, step forward.

00:06:29.110 --> 00:06:30.690
Two-on-two?

00:06:30.690 --> 00:06:32.350
A tag match.

00:06:32.970 --> 00:06:35.340
Be careful.  It could be a trap.

00:06:41.580 --> 00:06:46.030
Jonouchi, we must accept this duel.

00:06:46.030 --> 00:06:49.020
Yeah!  I'm looking forward to it!

00:06:52.480 --> 00:06:56.400
Welcome to our Labyrinth Field.

00:06:56.400 --> 00:06:59.860
Huh?  This doesn't look 
like a Labyrinth Field.

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:01.820
You'll see soon enough.

00:07:01.820 --> 00:07:04.000
Wager your Star Chips.

00:07:05.770 --> 00:07:07.010
I wager two.

00:07:07.010 --> 00:07:10.440
I wager four.  That's a total of six Chips.

00:07:10.440 --> 00:07:11.510
Understood.

00:07:11.510 --> 00:07:13.150
Let's do this, Jonouchi!

00:07:13.150 --> 00:07:16.820
If we win this duel, we'll 
both have ten Star Chips.

00:07:16.820 --> 00:07:18.750
We can enter Pegasus's castle.

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:19.770
Right!

00:07:19.770 --> 00:07:21.110
That won't happen.

00:07:21.110 --> 00:07:23.770
We're Player Killers of the labyrinth.

00:07:23.770 --> 00:07:26.620
We won't let you get back to the surface.

00:07:26.620 --> 00:07:28.400
Do your best, you two!

00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:30.730
Beat them so we can get out of here!

00:07:32.260 --> 00:07:34.670
Start the duel!

00:07:34.670 --> 00:07:38.350
It's my turn!  I play this card!

00:07:38.350 --> 00:07:40.240
Labyrinth Wall!

00:07:40.480 --> 00:07:43.740
Labyrinth Wall?  Those are walls of a maze.

00:07:47.770 --> 00:07:48.750
What's that?

00:07:48.750 --> 00:07:49.780
What's going on?

00:08:00.880 --> 00:08:02.190
What's this?

00:08:02.190 --> 00:08:07.640
Labyrinth Wall creates a Labyrinth Field.

00:08:07.640 --> 00:08:11.600
Welcome to our Labyrinth Field.

00:08:30.820 --> 00:08:32.010
Mokuba...

00:08:39.910 --> 00:08:44.880
Since my turn is done, 
I'll explain the rules.

00:08:45.340 --> 00:08:49.110
Each player begins with 
2000 Life Points as usual.

00:08:49.110 --> 00:08:55.860
But if either teammate loses all 
their Life Points, that team loses.

00:08:55.860 --> 00:08:59.850
So if I lose, so does Yugi.

00:08:59.850 --> 00:09:03.760
Each team alternate turns, as do the players.

00:09:03.760 --> 00:09:08.830
Next, I'll explain how to 
solve this Labyrinth Field.

00:09:08.830 --> 00:09:14.970
All monsters played on the field 
will be similar to chess pieces.

00:09:15.330 --> 00:09:22.710
If the monster is in attack position, it can move 
the same number of spaces as its Level during that turn.

00:09:24.570 --> 00:09:28.530
But if it loses in battle, it 
can't escape the labyrinth.

00:09:28.530 --> 00:09:36.480
If you win and exit the labyrinth, 
you can open one of the two doors.

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:41.950
It's your choice which door to go for.

00:09:41.950 --> 00:09:44.620
Choose the door that you think is correct.

00:09:44.620 --> 00:09:46.970
Hey, that's not fair!

00:09:46.970 --> 00:09:48.710
Our lives are on the line!

00:09:48.710 --> 00:09:52.000
Give us a hint on which door is correct!

00:09:52.930 --> 00:09:54.240
Fine.

00:09:54.240 --> 00:09:55.740
Starting now...

00:09:55.950 --> 00:09:58.740
...one of us will tell the truth.

00:09:59.490 --> 00:10:03.020
And the other will only tell lies.

00:10:06.290 --> 00:10:08.040
Oh my.

00:10:11.060 --> 00:10:17.260
Yugi boy, don't be angry over 
this unexpected surprise.

00:10:33.010 --> 00:10:37.460
Starting now, one of us will tell the truth.

00:10:37.460 --> 00:10:40.710
And the other will only tell lies.

00:10:46.780 --> 00:10:47.640
Hey.

00:10:48.570 --> 00:10:51.110
Were there any lies in what you just said?

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:53.730
No.  That's the truth.

00:10:55.810 --> 00:11:00.760
The correct door is my Mei door.

00:11:00.760 --> 00:11:05.860
No,the correct door is my Kyu door.

00:11:06.950 --> 00:11:09.680
Which one of them is telling the truth?

00:11:10.160 --> 00:11:11.200
Wait a sec.

00:11:11.540 --> 00:11:15.250
I heard a similar riddle before.

00:11:15.780 --> 00:11:22.170
A man stands at a fork in a road.  One road leads to a 
town of truth-tellers, and the other leads to a town of liars.

00:11:22.170 --> 00:11:27.820
A traveler asks a villager for directions, 
but he doesn't know which town he's from.

00:11:28.380 --> 00:11:33.950
The traveler wants to go to the town of 
truth-tellers, but he's only allowed to ask one question.

00:11:34.380 --> 00:11:38.540
The riddle is what he should 
ask.  The answer is...

00:11:38.880 --> 00:11:41.510
"Take me to your town."

00:11:42.040 --> 00:11:46.710
If the villager is a truth-teller, he'll 
take him to his own town of truth-tellers.

00:11:46.710 --> 00:11:51.120
If he's a liar, he'll lie and take 
him to the town of truth-tellers.

00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:55.150
In that case, answer my question!

00:11:55.150 --> 00:11:56.040
Fine.

00:11:56.040 --> 00:11:59.080
You each get to ask one question.

00:11:59.080 --> 00:12:05.600
If one of the doors is correct, 
tell me which door you're guarding.

00:12:05.600 --> 00:12:08.220
You... and you.

00:12:08.220 --> 00:12:10.130
Which door are you guarding?

00:12:12.850 --> 00:12:18.150
The truth-teller and the liar will 
both point to the correct door.

00:12:23.960 --> 00:12:25.220
All right!

00:12:27.160 --> 00:12:28.640
I did it, Yugi!

00:12:28.640 --> 00:12:30.930
The Kyu door is the correct one!

00:12:30.930 --> 00:12:33.680
Since we know which door 
we want, we got this!

00:12:36.310 --> 00:12:40.470
Is the Kyu door really the correct one?

00:12:40.750 --> 00:12:42.620
What's wrong, Yugi?

00:12:42.620 --> 00:12:44.040
You're still suspicious?

00:12:44.040 --> 00:12:47.980
From one point of view, 
your answer is correct.

00:12:48.960 --> 00:12:53.640
However, I'm not sure you can 
trust what they say so easily.

00:12:54.140 --> 00:12:55.640
What do you mean?

00:12:55.920 --> 00:13:00.470
I also know about the 
truth-telling town riddle.

00:13:00.470 --> 00:13:04.930
But it's dangerous to apply 
that to this situation.

00:13:06.270 --> 00:13:14.170
The riddle would be different if the 
traveler met two villagers instead of one.

00:13:14.170 --> 00:13:22.750
And if the two villagers said that one was from the 
truth-teller's town and the other was from the liar's town.

00:13:23.510 --> 00:13:25.580
That part is suspicious.

00:13:28.040 --> 00:13:33.730
If one was a liar, they'll both say that 
they're from the truth-teller's town.

00:13:34.100 --> 00:13:38.100
There's also the possibility 
that they're both liars.

00:13:38.620 --> 00:13:43.370
If so, there's no guarantee that 
there's a town on either road.

00:13:44.100 --> 00:13:46.110
I see.

00:13:46.310 --> 00:13:48.110
Let's continue the game.

00:13:48.110 --> 00:13:50.480
Don't be fooled by their words.

00:13:50.860 --> 00:13:53.610
We'll eventually figure 
out which door is correct.

00:13:53.610 --> 00:13:57.820
You're right.  There's no point 
worrying about it for now.

00:14:00.570 --> 00:14:02.000
Let's continue the duel.

00:14:02.730 --> 00:14:06.260
To defeat our opponents, 
we must enter the dungeon.

00:14:06.880 --> 00:14:08.170
My turn.

00:14:08.170 --> 00:14:11.150
I play Beaver Warrior in attack position.

00:14:15.070 --> 00:14:17.510
You can't attack us.

00:14:17.820 --> 00:14:20.470
Move your monster equal to its Level.

00:14:20.660 --> 00:14:22.220
It's Level 4.

00:14:22.220 --> 00:14:24.480
Beaver Warrior, move four spaces.

00:14:28.780 --> 00:14:32.570
You'll learn how terrifying 
the Labyrinth Field is.

00:14:32.570 --> 00:14:34.320
It's my turn.

00:14:34.320 --> 00:14:42.220
I play Shadow Ghoul and Polymerization 
to fuse it with Labyrinth Wall.

00:14:42.880 --> 00:14:44.000
What?

00:14:46.130 --> 00:14:46.970
What's this?

00:14:50.500 --> 00:14:54.410
Wall Shadow, Labyrinth Slash!

00:14:56.380 --> 00:14:58.380
Beaver Warrior is destroyed.

00:15:01.730 --> 00:15:03.510
What is that?

00:15:08.800 --> 00:15:10.120
Wall Shadow?

00:15:10.120 --> 00:15:13.150
That wasn't fair!  You can't do that!

00:15:13.150 --> 00:15:14.350
It was perfectly fair.

00:15:14.350 --> 00:15:17.820
Wall Shadow didn't move any 
spaces.  It moved on the wall.

00:15:17.820 --> 00:15:21.200
There are no spaces on the wall.

00:15:22.590 --> 00:15:29.880
Wall Shadow can freely move along the labyrinth 
walls and destroy its enemy with a single swipe.

00:15:30.680 --> 00:15:32.620
It's a powerful enemy.

00:15:33.110 --> 00:15:37.730
This labyrinth is like a giant 
monster that you're trapped inside.

00:15:37.730 --> 00:15:41.550
Correct.  You'll never escape 
this labyrinth alive.

00:15:42.310 --> 00:15:44.060
It's my turn.

00:15:44.260 --> 00:15:46.570
I play Axe Raider in attack position.

00:15:47.930 --> 00:15:50.710
I set another card on the field.

00:15:54.920 --> 00:16:02.110
But since it can't attack an enemy that 
it can't see, it won't move this turn.

00:16:02.110 --> 00:16:05.210
It'll wait here and stay away from the wall.

00:16:05.210 --> 00:16:09.210
Therefore, it'll be ready to attack 
at any moment.  How's that?

00:16:09.390 --> 00:16:11.630
Good, Jonouchi.

00:16:11.630 --> 00:16:16.750
As long as you stay away from the wall, 
you can avoid Wall Shadow's attacks.

00:16:16.750 --> 00:16:20.190
Yugi, watch my strategy.

00:16:20.190 --> 00:16:24.170
I hope Jonouchi doesn't screw up.

00:16:24.170 --> 00:16:27.550
Don't worry.  Yugi will back him up.

00:16:27.550 --> 00:16:29.020
I hope you're right.

00:16:29.640 --> 00:16:34.530
In a tag match, they can gang 
up on the weaker of the two.

00:16:34.530 --> 00:16:36.420
My turn.

00:16:36.420 --> 00:16:38.480
I set one card.

00:16:38.480 --> 00:16:41.080
This is the trap card Jirai Gumo.

00:16:42.230 --> 00:16:49.910
If you enter the labyrinth and land on 
certain spaces, Jirai Gumo will destroy it.

00:16:50.350 --> 00:16:55.460
I also play Labyrinth Tank in attack 
position and move it seven spaces.

00:17:03.230 --> 00:17:06.440
You can no longer escape from this labyrinth.

00:17:06.440 --> 00:17:08.040
I end my turn.

00:17:08.040 --> 00:17:09.150
It's my turn.

00:17:11.970 --> 00:17:14.620
I play Celtic Guardian in attack position.

00:17:17.180 --> 00:17:19.720
It moves four spaces into the labyrinth.

00:17:20.900 --> 00:17:25.640
Celtic Guardian has fewer attack 
points than Wall Shadow.

00:17:25.640 --> 00:17:27.020
It'll also be destroyed.

00:17:27.020 --> 00:17:29.240
You fool.  It's my turn.

00:17:29.240 --> 00:17:31.160
Wall Shadow attacks.

00:17:31.260 --> 00:17:33.230
Attack Celtic Guardian!

00:17:36.000 --> 00:17:37.730
It'll die in vain.

00:17:37.730 --> 00:17:40.170
Celtic Guardian is finished!

00:17:45.240 --> 00:17:46.180
You fell for it.

00:17:46.180 --> 00:17:47.200
What?

00:17:49.150 --> 00:17:50.440
What's this?

00:17:50.880 --> 00:17:52.650
Kunai with Chain.

00:17:52.970 --> 00:17:56.800
Impossible!  He captured Wall Shadow?

00:17:58.040 --> 00:18:03.600
I set the card Kunai with Chain, 
which captures an attacking monster.

00:18:03.600 --> 00:18:06.840
I played this trap card to help Yugi.

00:18:06.840 --> 00:18:13.340
Celtic Guardian also gains 500 attack 
points, so it's now stronger than Wall Shadow.

00:18:20.410 --> 00:18:22.480
Wall Shadow is destroyed!

00:18:24.420 --> 00:18:25.730
They did it!

00:18:25.730 --> 00:18:28.970
Yeah.  They're a good combo.

00:18:28.970 --> 00:18:33.160
Jonouchi, you really have become stronger.

00:18:33.160 --> 00:18:36.440
This battle has only begun.

00:18:36.750 --> 00:18:39.370
That's right!  Let's continue the duel!

00:18:39.820 --> 00:18:43.870
We'll show you that we're 
the greatest tag team.

00:18:43.870 --> 00:18:45.420
Let's go, Yugi!

00:18:45.420 --> 00:18:48.640
Yeah!  We'll win with the power of teamwork!

00:18:55.240 --> 00:18:56.920
Fantastic.

00:18:56.920 --> 00:18:59.080
That was wonderful.

00:18:59.080 --> 00:19:02.000
I can't wait to see what happens next.

00:19:04.710 --> 00:19:05.860
Pardon me.

00:19:07.130 --> 00:19:09.910
We've been searching for Kaiba...

00:19:10.270 --> 00:19:14.300
I can tell that you haven't found him yet.

00:19:14.300 --> 00:19:16.030
I'm terribly sorry.

00:19:16.030 --> 00:19:18.530
We are continuing our search.

00:19:18.530 --> 00:19:20.570
Please wait a bit longer.

00:19:21.530 --> 00:19:23.060
I don't mind.

00:19:23.060 --> 00:19:27.240
Kaiba boy will come here sooner or later.

00:19:27.950 --> 00:19:29.420
He definitely will.

00:19:35.950 --> 00:19:37.730
Pull yourself together!

00:19:37.730 --> 00:19:41.550
I can't lose heart.  It'll be fine.

00:19:41.550 --> 00:19:44.260
My brother will come for me.

00:19:44.260 --> 00:19:44.970
That's right.

00:19:46.140 --> 00:19:47.960
Give it back!

00:19:47.960 --> 00:19:52.100
My brother has always come for me.

00:19:58.060 --> 00:20:01.020
Big brother, I won't give in.

00:20:02.000 --> 00:20:04.620
I won't give him the key.

00:20:05.240 --> 00:20:09.020
I'll protect Kaiba Corporation.

00:20:13.280 --> 00:20:16.480
I'm coming, Mokuba.

00:20:32.240 --> 00:20:38.450
Yugi and Jonouchi destroy the traps in 
the Labyrinth Field with their combos.

00:20:38.450 --> 00:20:42.910
You're awesome!  With your teamwork, 
you'll quickly escape this labyrinth!

00:20:42.910 --> 00:20:46.170
But they won't let us win so easily.

00:20:46.170 --> 00:20:49.500
Look!  A gigantic monster is 
coming out of the three boxes!

00:20:49.500 --> 00:20:53.070
That's Gate Guardian, the 
Labyrinth Brothers' trump card!

00:20:53.070 --> 00:20:56.740
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Three Gods Combine!
Gate Guardian

00:20:56.740 --> 00:20:58.570
Duel, standby!

00:21:01.620 --> 00:21:10.020
The flask glistens

00:21:11.060 --> 00:21:17.870
Wait for me in the science classroom

00:21:18.360 --> 00:21:26.850
If we put our cold hands together

00:21:27.550 --> 00:21:34.620
And rub them together, they become warm

00:21:36.320 --> 00:21:40.450
Shower of happiness

00:21:40.740 --> 00:21:44.570
I will shower you with it

00:21:44.890 --> 00:21:52.840
I will support you even when you feel lonely

00:21:53.040 --> 00:21:57.080
Shower of happiness

00:21:57.340 --> 00:22:01.200
You are not alone

